From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375: mark the GPU SMMU as an adreno SMMU

Userspace hits this on the first DRM_IOCTL_MSM_GET_PARAM:

  WARNING: msm_iommu_pagetable_create ... "No per-process page tables"
    msm_iommu_pagetable_create+0x278/0x294
    a6xx_create_private_vm+0x28/0x74
    msm_gpu_create_private_vm+0x38/0x120
    msm_context_vm+0x58/0x80
    adreno_get_param+0x38/0x31c

so every context falls back to sharing one address space.

arm-smmu-qcom only installs the Adreno implementation, which is what
provides the adreno_smmu_priv interface used for per-process page tables,
when the SMMU node claims to be one:

	if (np && of_device_is_compatible(np, "qcom,adreno-smmu"))
		impl = data->adreno_impl;
	else
		impl = data->impl;

The pieces are already in place: "qcom,sm6375-smmu-v2" is in
qcom_smmu_impl_of_match[] pointing at qcom_smmu_v2_data, which does have
.adreno_impl = &qcom_adreno_smmu_v2_impl, and qcom_adreno_can_do_ttbr1()
only refuses msm8996, so an SMMU v2 is fine here. Only the compatible was
missing, matching what sm6115.dtsi already does for its GPU SMMU.

This went unnoticed for the same reason as the catalog mismatch: no
upstream device tree enables the SM6375 GPU, so this SMMU was never used
by the GPU.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
@@ -1487,7 +1487,8 @@
 		};
 
 		adreno_smmu: iommu@5940000 {
-			compatible = "qcom,sm6375-smmu-v2", "qcom,smmu-v2";
+			compatible = "qcom,sm6375-smmu-v2", "qcom,adreno-smmu",
+				     "qcom,smmu-v2";
 			reg = <0 0x05940000 0 0x10000>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 			#global-interrupts = <2>;
